      "side": 1,
      "message": "Initial pass, I\u0027m not too fond of adding the new API for this. Do you already have metrics on how often the `Flush` calls are happening and how much time we are spending in them? This feels like a pretty big hammer solution.\n\nI\u0027m wondering if it would be possible to do this internally in Dawn instead, i.e. have Dawn decide when to actually call the `Flush` instead of relying on an external signal. Or alternatively, make Dawn know when it doesn\u0027t need to flush yet, and wait until something that comes in needs to be flush and then calling `Flush` then?",
      "revId": "5e7d227759c004e3a1e5606db9c48c2ca911f20d",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
